tools.description:
PixelLab AI-powered pixel art generation service.

Use of this service is subject to PixelLab's Terms of Service:
https://pixellab.ai/termsofservice

This MCP server provides programmatic access to generate:
- Characters with multiple directional views
- Character animations
- Isometric tiles
- Top-down tilesets for game maps
- Sidescroller tilesets for platformer games

All generation operations are non-blocking and return job IDs for status tracking.
Requires PixelLab subscription (with credit fallback support).

**Pixel tools (free, exact, you are the artist)**: one command line, pixelart_workbench(argv=[...]), inspects, edits, draws and animates pixel art by your own decisions; combine it with the AI tools above. Start with pixelart_workbench(argv=['describe', 'start'], mode='low'|'high') — low acts directly with few tokens, high plans out loud and reviews every frame. Animated effects (spells, hits, explosions, auras): vfx_workbench(argv=['describe', 'start']) — same ids, exports to the user's My effects.

**Git access**: Clone and push game project source code with standard git.
Use `list_projects` to see your projects and their git clone URLs.

Generate a freeform pixel-art image with the Pixen model.

Pixen is the newer of the two fast generators and holds up better on small
sprites. Pick between the three text-to-image tools like this:
- create_image_pixflux — when you need an init image (img2img), a palette
  given as an image, isometric, or shading control.
- create_image_pixen — this one; cleaner small sprites, bigger canvas.
- create_image_pro — best quality, returns a set of candidates, costs more;
  takes a palette as hex colours (1-bit, Game Boy, PICO-8, NES, Lospec).

Canvas: 16-768 per side and each side must be a multiple of 4; total area
16x16 to 512x512. Below 32 the canvas must be SQUARE, so the small sizes
are 16x16, 20x20, 24x24 and 28x28.

Cost: 1 generation. Generation time: ~10-40 seconds (async).
Poll with get_image(job_id).

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__pixellab__create_image_pixen(args: {
  // What to draw (e.g. 'ornate iron key', 'mossy stone wall').
  description: string;
  // Detail level (weakly guiding).
  detail?: "low detail" | "medium detail" | "highly detailed";
  // Which way the subject faces (weakly guiding).
  direction?: "north" | "north-east" | "east" | "south-east" | "south" | "south-west" | "west" | "north-west";
  // Canvas height in pixels. Must be a multiple of 4; height must equal width when either side is below 32.
  height?: number;
  // Return the subject on a transparent background. True for sprites and items, False for scenes. Up to 256x256 of area (65,536 px, e.g. 256x256 or 512x128); larger canvases are refused with it on.
  no_background?: boolean;
  // Outline style (weakly guiding).
  outline?: "single color black outline" | "single color outline" | "selective outline" | "lineless";
  // Internal Game Builder project context; the finished image is linked after generation.
  project_id?: string | null;
  // Seed for reproducible generation.
  seed?: number | null;
  // Camera angle (weakly guiding).
  view?: "side" | "low top-down" | "high top-down";
  // Canvas width in pixels. Must be a multiple of 4; width must equal height when either side is below 32. width x height may not exceed 512x512 = 262,144, so the widest canvases are e.g. 768x340 or 680x384, not 768x384.
  width?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

